      "result": "All 16 checklist items are recorded and confirmed complete (16/16).\n\n**Summary of results:** 14 PASS, 2 FAIL.\n\nThe two failures identified:\n- **IX-16 (FAIL)** — Clicking a knowledge graph node only highlights/selects it visually; it never opens the corresponding document or switches to the Documents tab, and no \"View Document\" affordance exists.\n- **IX-17 (FAIL)** — Clicking a reference link inside a collapsed content section correctly avoids navigating away, but no prompt/toast informs the user they need to expand the section first — this feedback is silently missing.\n\nAll other items (FT-1 through FT-10, CS-12, CS-13, IX-15, IX-18) passed with verified DOM/accessibility-tree evidence, including the more involved FT-9 (cross-tab state persistence for selected document, section expand/collapse state, and graph zoom) and FT-10 (favorites real-time count, filter/sort survival, dedicated favorites view, and reload persistence), both confirmed clean on isolated retest.",
